Package: RdistNN
Title: Distributional Nearest-Neighbor Inference for Local Conditional Moment Models
Version: 0.1.0.9001
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Jakob", family = "Juergens", email = "info@jakobjuergens.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Jakob Juergens [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Jakob Juergens <info@jakobjuergens.com>
Description: Implements distributional nearest-neighbor weights and
    diagnostics for local conditional moment and Z-estimation problems.
    The initial public release focuses on nonparametric regression and
    conditional average treatment effects, with delete-one jackknife standard
    errors, tuning-grid diagnostics, visualization, and study-specific
    replication workflows for the affine conditional Z-estimation paper.
    Conditional LATE from supplied nuisance predictions, partially linear
    quantile-regression moment evaluation and local IV-GMM functionality
    are experimental.
    Lower-level generalized U-statistic and jackknife utilities are included
    as supporting infrastructure. Uses compiled C++ fast paths with robust
    batched R fallbacks for supported algorithms; source installation still
    requires a C++17 toolchain. The package also includes estimator-specific
    inference routes, including delete-one jackknife
    diagnostics and direct sandwich covariance estimates.
